  "text": "Thank you all three. These are exactly the kinds of material issues I needed to hear before authorizing. Let me summarize what I'm taking away: Thomas, the separation agreement's exclusive forum clause may require us to file in state court in the county where the executive worked rather than federal court — that needs to be resolved before we commit to a venue. Nadia, your forensic review only confirmed copying of the customer-list database, not pricing materials or source-code documentation — so seeking broad relief covering all three categories could overreach and undermine our credibility with the court. Owen, the carrier's written consent is a prerequisite to preserving coverage, and we cannot file without it. I want to address all three before I sign any authorization. Thomas — please add the forum clause to the strategy memorandum and advise whether it constrains our filing venue. Nadia — please update the evidence chart to reflect that only the customer-list database was confirmed copied, so we can reassess the scope of relief. Owen — please get the carrier's written consent into the litigation file and confirm it before I authorize filing. I am not authorizing the preliminary injunction today. We will reconvene once these prerequisites are addressed."
}
